.TH SHARDPOSTCTL-SUBMISSION 1 "2026-10-02" "ShardPost 0.43.0" "ShardPost Manual"
.SH NAME
shardpostctl-submission \- list and cancel delayed JMAP submissions of an account
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shardpostctl submission list
.RB [ \-json ]
.I account
.br
.B shardpostctl submission cancel
.RB [ \-json ]
.I account
.I id
.SH DESCRIPTION
A JMAP client can ask for a message to be released later (EmailSubmission
with the FUTURERELEASE parameter HOLDFOR or HOLDUNTIL). Such a submission
waits in the submission queue of the cluster until its release time;
then a worker sends a copy of the message that was taken when it was
created. These commands show the submissions an account has waiting and
cancel one for the user.
.PP
Delayed sending is offered with
.IR jmap.submission.delayed.max_delay_seconds ;
the queue needs the admin store indexes
.RI ( admin.kv_index
.B write
or
.BR read ).
Without them both commands fail with exit status 75.
.SS submission list
Lists the submissions the account still holds a message copy for, by
release time: pending, being sent, or ended and not yet cleaned up. Each
line names the submission id, its state
.RB ( pending ,
.BR sending ,
.BR final ,
.BR canceled ,
.BR failed ),
the release time, the attempts so far, the size and the envelope. The
list is read from the account's own records, without a listing of the
cluster. Role:
.BR diagnose .
.SS submission cancel
Cancels a pending submission as a JMAP client would (undoStatus
canceled): the message is not sent, its copy is deleted, and the user's
EmailSubmission shows
.BR canceled .
The record names who canceled it
.RB ( admin: \fIidentity\fR).
A submission that the worker has begun to send cannot be canceled any
more (exit status 65); one that has ended and was cleaned up is not
found (exit status 67). Tell the user: their client shows the
submission as canceled. Role:
.BR support .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-json
Print the answer as JSON.
.SH EXAMPLES
A user asks why a message they scheduled has not gone out yet:
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl submission list user@example.org
.RE
.fi
.PP
The user scheduled a message to the wrong recipients and cannot reach
their client; cancel it:
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl submission cancel user@example.org S5f0c1e2d3b4a5f6e7d8c9b0a
.RE
.fi
.PP
Before going back to a release older than 0.43.0 the queue has to be
empty; find what an account still has waiting, as JSON:
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl submission list -json user@example.org | jq -r '.items[] | "\e(.id) \e(.state) \e(.release)"'
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Done.
.TP
.B 64
Wrong arguments, or the account or id is not valid.
.TP
.B 65
The submission is no longer pending (it is being sent or has been sent).
.TP
.B 67
No such submission (it may have ended).
.TP
.B 70
An unexpected answer from the server.
.TP
.B 75
The server cannot be reached, or it has no submission queue (try again,
or check
.IR admin.kv_index ).
.TP
.B 77
The caller lacks the role
.B diagnose
(list) or
.B support
(cancel), or may not address the account.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shardpostctl (1),
.BR shardpostctl-account (1)
.PP
Delayed sending is described in
.IR docs/jmap.md ,
its settings in
.IR docs/configuration.md ,
its operation and the rollback rule in
.IR docs/operations/README.md .
